    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for rust-keylime",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for rust-keylime fixes the following issue:\n\n- CVE-2026-115905: zip: security control bypass via parser differential between central directory and local headers\n  (bsc#1287921)\n- CVE-2026-115906: zip: authentication bypass in AES encrypted entries due to improper HMAC verification (bsc#1287921)\n- CVE-2026-115907: zip: denial of service via unbounded memory allocation in legacy decoders (bsc#1287921)\n- CVE-2026-115908: zip: path traversal via lexical symlink validation during extraction (bsc#1287921)\n- CVE-2026-115909: zip: denial of service via uncontrolled memory allocation on symlink targets (bsc#1287921)\n\nChanges for rust-keylime:\n\n- Update to version 0.2.10+12:\n * log Agent UUID at push agent startup\n * Limit actix-web workers\n * Fix clippy needless_late_init warnings\n * Unwrap OCTET STRING wrapped EK certificates\n * build(deps): bump rand from 0.9.4 to 0.10.1\n * build(deps): bump glob from 0.3.3 to 0.3.4\n * build(deps): bump reqwest from 0.13.3 to 0.13.4\n * Check shutdown marker inside ml_extend loop\n * Fix clippy useless_borrows_in_formatting warnings\n * build(deps): bump tokio from 1.52.2 to 1.53.1\n * Fix payload key upgrade regression by falling back to mTLS key\n * Accept any RSA key size for payload encryption\n * Bump version to 0.2.10\n * keylime: use runtime OpenSSL algorithm detection instead of compile-time symbols\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "details",
        "text": "SUSE-2026-4931,SUSE-SLE-Micro-5.5-2026-4931",
        "title": "Patchnames"
      },
